def make_ei_prompt(page_number: int, total_pages: int) -> str:
    return f"""This is page {page_number} of {total_pages} from a pharmaceutical vendor \
elemental impurity (EI) declaration form (ICH Q3D).

STEP 1 — IDENTIFY THE CONCENTRATION UNIT (CRITICAL):
Look very carefully at the column header, the table title, and any footnotes to
determine the UNIT of the reported concentrations. The unit is usually one of:
  ppm, µg/g, mg/kg   (these are all equivalent — 1 ppm = 1 µg/g)
  ppb, ng/g, µg/kg   (these are 1000× SMALLER — 1 ppb = 0.001 ppm)
  %  or  w/w%        (these are 10000× LARGER — 1% = 10000 ppm)
  mg/g               (1000× larger — 1 mg/g = 1000 ppm)
DO NOT ASSUME ppm. If the header says ppb (or ng/g or µg/kg), you MUST report
concentration_unit as "ppb". Reporting the wrong unit causes a 1000× error.
Report the exact unit string you see for EACH element in concentration_unit.

STEP 2 — FIND THE LOQ / REPORTING LIMIT:
Look for a "Limit", "LOQ", "Reporting Limit", or "<" threshold in the column
header or footnote (e.g. "<0.30 ppm", "LOQ = 0.05 ppm"). Record as page_loq
together with its unit (page_loq_unit). If none stated, set page_loq to 0.

STEP 3 — READ EVERY ELEMENT ROW (report value in the unit AS PRINTED):
1. ACTUAL NUMBER printed (e.g. "1.25", "0.50", "285") → use that exact number,
   and set concentration_unit to the column's unit (could be ppm OR ppb).
2. "<X.XX" or "≤X.XX" → use X.XX as the value, set observed_level to "<X.XX".
3. "BDL (0.034 ppm)" or "BLQ (0.05)" (bracketed limit) → use the bracketed number
   0.034 as the value; set observed_level to the full raw text "BDL (0.034 ppm)".
4. "BDL" / "BLQ" / "Below LOQ" with NO bracketed number → use page_loq if known,
   else 0; set observed_level to the raw text.
5. "ND" / "Not Detected" / "Below LOD" / "<LOD" → value 0.0; observed_level "ND".
6. "NA" / "N/A" / blank / "Not Tested" → value 0.0; observed_level "Not tested".
7. Multiple batch result columns → take the MAXIMUM across batches.
8. Intentionally-added elements → still extract the value, never skip.
9. "% of Perm. Conc." / "% of Permitted Concentration" / "<30% of Perm. Conc."
   / "meets Option 1" (results reported as a PERCENTAGE of the ICH Q3D permitted
   concentration, common on Roquette CoAs): DO NOT convert to a number and DO NOT
   treat the "%" as a concentration unit. Set concentration_value to the numeric
   percentage (0 if none is printed), concentration_unit to "% of permitted", and
   copy the FULL phrase verbatim into observed_level (e.g. "<30% of Perm. Conc.").
   This is a QUALITATIVE below-limit declaration: the downstream system uses a
   value of ZERO for it in the risk assessment (ICH Q3D / DRL convention) — it is
   NOT a measured number.

ALWAYS set observed_level to the EXACT raw text in the result cell (including the
"<", "BDL", brackets, "% of Perm. Conc.", and any unit). This is the audit trail.

Also extract per-element: intentionally_added (Yes/No), listed_in_coa (Yes/No),
analytical_method (ICP-MS/ICP-OES/AAS), comments (footnotes).

STEP 4 — SPECIAL TABLE LAYOUTS (read the RIGHT column):
A) TWO NUMERIC COLUMNS — "Content measured or range" AND "Report Limit (RL)"
   (e.g. Peter Greven / Ligamed magnesium stearate CoAs):
   - The RESULT is the "Content measured or range" column. If it shows a number
     (e.g. "~2030"), that number is the value; set observed_level to it and
     concentration_unit to the table's unit (often ppb).
   - Only when the Content cell is "<RL" / "below RL" / empty do you fall back to
     the "Report Limit (RL)" value (worst case); set observed_level to "<RL"
     and the value to the RL number.
   - NEVER report the Report Limit as the result when a measured Content exists.
B) DRL API ELEMENTAL DECLARATION (header names "Dr. Reddy's Laboratories" or
   "DECLARATION OF RESIDUES OF ELEMENTAL IMPURITIES", often 3 batch columns and a
   LOD/LOQ column):
   - If the batch cells show numbers, take the MAXIMUM across the batches.
   - If every batch shows "Below LOD" / "BLOD" / "Not Detected", set
     observed_level to "Below LOD" (the system treats a true LOD non-detect as 0).
   - If batches show "Below LOQ" / "<LOQ", use the LOQ value (bracketed or the
     LOD/LOQ column) as a conservative worst case.
C) "NOT ANALYSED" / "NOT TESTED" / "NA" cell WHEN the same document ALSO carries a
   vendor statement that the element is not intentionally added and the material
   meets ICH Q3D Option 1: report observed_level as "meets Option 1" for that
   element (the system treats this qualitative Option-1 compliance statement as a
   value of ZERO). If NO such control statement exists, leave it as "Not tested".

Return ONLY valid JSON — no markdown, no explanation:
{{
  "page_loq": 0.30,
  "page_loq_unit": "ppm",
  "elements": [
    {{
      "symbol": "Pb",
      "name": "Lead",
      "class": "1",
      "concentration_value": 285,
      "concentration_unit": "ppb",
      "observed_level": "285 ppb",
      "analytical_method": "ICP-MS",
      "intentionally_added": "No",
      "listed_in_coa": "Yes",
      "comments": ""
    }}
  ]
}}"""


